adminWorld.voiceCapacityHint:
Voice is push-to-talk (PTT) half-duplex relay; a 60s voice message is ~240KB (~43kbps incl. base64 overhead). CPU load is minimal — bandwidth is the bottleneck.
· 10 users in conversation (~3 speaking at once): server egress ≈ 1.3Mbps; minimum config 1 vCPU / 2GB RAM / 3Mbps is enough;
· 20 users: ≈ 2.6Mbps; 2 vCPU / 4GB RAM / 5Mbps+ bandwidth recommended;
· Meaning of the limit: at most N people can talk at the same time within 30m; others automatically fall back to text mode.
